From 6430143a79b596b54414e99393cde6ee1cf1699c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mechres <164776284+Mechres@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:41:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: hdmi: Add HDMI audio support

The A10/A31 HDMI block takes 32-bit PCM sub-frames through a FIFO port
fed by a dedicated DMA request line, but the driver never used it. Add
the pieces needed to play audio over HDMI:

 - an hdmi-codec through the DRM HDMI audio helper, whose prepare/
   shutdown callbacks program the audio module (reset, DMA mode, format,
   ACR N/CTS, channel status), start and stop the audio related packet
   and write the audio infoframe,
 - an ASoC CPU DAI with a dmaengine PCM on the FIFO port, and a sound
   card tying it to the codec,
 - plug notifications so the codec picks up the sink's ELD.

Only 2 channel S16_LE/S24_LE at 32, 44.1 and 48 kHz is offered: the
FIFO drains too slowly above 48 kHz. AUD_FIFO_CLEAR is a level, not a
pulse; leaving it set keeps the FIFO empty and the stream ends
instantly.

The packet arbiter setup moves into sun4i_hdmi_update_packets() so that
the audio packets can be added and removed while video is running; it
also no longer inherits stray polarity bits from the timing register.

Tested on an A31s tablet against a monitor with speakers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
